  "question": "LATEST CUSTOMER MESSAGE (the one to work on):\ncontacts made on 9/22 and after are not receiving follow up emails that are built in the sequences\n\nSCREENSHOTS ATTACHED TO THE LATEST MESSAGE (what the customer's screen showed, as read by an image model: context for the message, not part of what they wrote):\n[Screenshot the customer attached, as read by an image model]\nScreen: Campaign Performance Trend analytics chart\nWhat stands out: A tooltip is showing data points for 2026-09-24.\n\nEARLIER TURNS (context only: they resolve what \"it\", \"that\" or a follow-up refers to while the subject is the same, and do not carry over once the latest message changes subject. Only recent messages are shown and some may be cut, so a detail missing here is not proof the customer never gave it):\nCustomer: why is this campaign not sending follow up sequences?\n\ncampaign name:\nName 1\nSupport: Your campaign itself looks healthy: it's active, there's no error recorded, and your 9 sending inboxes are all connected. Sends have been going out most days (for example 147 on Oct 5), though Oct 2 shows 0 sent with no problem recorded for that day.\n\nOn the follow-up side, prospects like Name 7, Name 8, and Name 11 show a pending follow-up, but there's no next follow-up time currently set for them. That matches what you're seeing, follow-ups aren't being scheduled.\n\nTo fix this, check the campaign's sequence builder and the AI SDR Agent settings page to confirm the follow-up steps and resources are actually active, since a pending follow-up with no scheduled time usually points back to a step or setting there.\n\nWhat couldn't be checked: why the follow-up time isn't being set, whether your regular sequence steps are configured and enabled, and there was no live calendar or send test, only saved settings data. If you want, you can use the Record my screen button here to show me the sequence builder and AI SDR settings so we can narrow down what's off.\nCustomer: I am referring to the next steps in the sequence. Only the first email is deploying, but Step 2 and Step 3 are not sending\nSupport: Looking at the example thread, step 1 is scheduled for Oct 6, step 2 for Oct 13, and step 3 for Oct 20, none of them marked as skipped. So this isn't that steps 2 and 3 failed to send, it's that their scheduled dates haven't arrived yet, and step 1 is also still pending rather than already gone out. Nothing has actually failed to send as of this check.\n\nWhat's worth watching is whether step 1 actually sends once Oct 6 arrives. If it doesn't go out on or around that date, that would point to a real problem with the sequence rather than just timing.\n\nWhat couldn't be checked: whether these pending steps will actually fire when their scheduled time comes, and why the thread's next follow-up time shows as empty even though the individual steps have scheduled dates. There was no live send-dispatch or calendar check available, only the saved step data.\nCustomer: emails started sending Sept 22, step 2 was supposed to send 2 days later\nSupport: The thread I can see doesn't match that timing. For Name 7, step 0 went out on Oct 2, and steps 1, 2, and 3 are scheduled for later dates, roughly a week apart, not 2 days, and none are marked skipped. There's no record tying a Sept 22 start or a 2-day step-2 gap to this campaign or thread.\n\nIt's possible you're thinking of a different prospect, thread, or campaign than the one I'm looking at. Could you give me the exact name or email of the prospect you're seeing the Sept 22 start and 2-day gap for? That will let me check the right thread.",
